      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ورّد ثَوْبَهُ</span></b>  (tropical:)  [<i>He dyed his garment,</i> or <i>piece
of cloth, red,</i> or <i>of a rose-colour</i>]. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ورّدتِ الشَّجَرَةُ</span>, (AHn, L, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوْرِيدٌ</span>; (K;)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرَدَتْ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَردُ</span>; (Msb;) <i>The tree flowered,</i>
or <i>blossomed.</i> (AHn, L, Msb, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ورّدت</span> (tropical:)  <i>She</i>
(a woman) <i>reddened her cheek with the dye of
dyed cotton.</i> (L.)

